17592186436988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437013 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e83f4999-419d-51c4-a803-c6789f4e1b52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437014 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e9f85d81-d1f0-5077-ba52-dc9b36b72fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437015 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe5a3950-f690-5d04-879c-231b6f838613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $∇h(x,y,z)$ at $(1,-2,2)$ if $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3edc7251-4f74-5afa-bcee-22e839f081a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437016 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2x{z}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2z-2xy \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+2yz) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}z+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y,z) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y,z),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y,z),\\,{h}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2x{z}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,2z-2xy,\\,2{x}^{2}z+2y⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,-2,2) & =⟨2(1)(2)^{2}-(-2)^{2},\\,-2(1)(-2)+2(2),\\,2(1)^{2}(2)+2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8-4,4+4,4-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,8,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $∇f(x,y)$ at $(e,1)$ if $f(x,y)={x}^{y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51a75799-7672-5c71-a422-88f2c2c1de7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437017 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{y}) \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{y}) \\\\  & ={x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\text{ }i+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{ }j, \\\\ ∇f(e,1) & =1(e)^{1-1}\\,i+{e}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡e\\,j \\\\  & =i+e\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71515" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y)$ if $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}$ and $h(x,y)=y{e}^{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5961ee6e-358e-5baa-837e-dbd941cc54b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437018 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=f\\,∇\\,h+h\\,∇\\,f\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y})={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y})=x{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})=y{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\text{ }j=y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =x{e}^{y}(y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x}\\text{ }j)+y{e}^{x}({e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =xy{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j+y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+xy{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(x+1)y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+x(1+y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $∇h(x,y)$ at $(1,-1)$ if $h(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bace43f6-9821-5763-9bf8-9ca1cf7da037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437019 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}) \\\\  & =(2x+y){e}^{{x}^{2}+xy} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2x+y){e}^{{x}^{2}+xy},\\,x{e}^{{x}^{2}+xy}⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,-1) & =⟨(2(1)+(-1)){e}^{{1}^{2}+(1)(-1)},\\,1\\cdot {e}^{{1}^{2}+(1)(-1)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3503a39-2405-5c8f-9ad7-2d39b5c187d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437020 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =2x-2{y}^{2} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =4z-4yx \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4yz-2{z}^{2}-2{y}^{2}x) \\\\  & =4y-4z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=2(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+4(z-yx)\\,j+4(y-z)\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+4(z-yx)\\,j+4(y-z)\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-{y}^{2}=0, \\\\ z-yx=0, \\\\ y-z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation gives $x={y}^{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain $z={y}^{3}.$ Substituting $z={y}^{3}$ into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y=-1,$ we get $x=(-1)^{2}=1$ and $z=(-1)^{3}=-1.$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we obtain $x={0}^{2}=0$ and $z={0}^{3}=0.$\n\n- For $y=1,$ gives $x={1}^{2}=1$ and $z={1}^{3}=1.$\n\nFinally, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at three points: $(1,-1,-1),$ $(0,0,0)$ and $(1,1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d13fce5d-8bd4-547a-afec-720ff5befaa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437021 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =xy{e}^{x}+y{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =y(x+1){e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =x{e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =0+2z{e}^{z}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z} \\\\  & =z(2+z){e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y(x+1){e}^{x}=0 \\\\ x{e}^{x}=0 \\\\ z(2+z){e}^{z}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation gives $x=0.$ Substituting these into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0+1){e}^{0} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the third equation, we get  $z=0$ or $z=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,-2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
